OpenTelemetry: Requests of Portal | php can now be found and followed in a tracing backend: a sampled request returns its trace ID in the response header @X-Trace-Id@, the server span carries the Keycloak subject of the logged in user as @user.id@ and keeps its route name when the HTTP cache is enabled, and log records written during a sampled request carry @trace_id@ and @span_id@. The OAuth @code@ and @session_state@ of the Keycloak callback are no longer recorded in the span. Health probes, requests of the Blackbox exporter and console commands can be excluded from tracing, see the OpenTelemetry documentation.